section: language
issues: #24848
mrs: !16783
synopsis: Introduce the :extension:`MeaningfulMainReturn` extension and :ghc-flag:`-Wambiguous-main-return`
description:
  The new warning flag :ghc-flag:`-Wambiguous-main-return`, which is enabled by
  default, will warn if the ``main`` function's result type doesn't unify with
  either ``()`` or ``Void``. For example: ::

    main :: IO Int
    main = pure 42

  This warning will only be emitted if the new :extension:`MeaningfulMainReturn`
  extension is disabled.

  If :extension:`MeaningfulMainReturn` is enabled, programs with a ``main``
  function whose result type doesn't unify with either ``()``, ``Void``, or
  ``ExitCode`` will be rejected.

  Additionally, if it can be determined that ``main`` returns an ``ExitCode``,
  the value returned will be the program's exit code: ::

    {-# LANGUAGE MeaningfulMainReturn #-}
    import System.Exit

    main :: IO ExitCode
    main = pure (ExitFailure 42)

  The above behaves as if the user had written: ::

    {-# LANGUAGE NoMeaningfulMainReturn #-}
    import System.Exit

    main :: IO ()
    main = pure (ExitFailure 42) >>= exitWith

  :extension:`MeaningfulMainReturn` is intended to become the default in the
  next GHC language edition.

  This implements `GHC Proposal #631
  <https://ghc-proposals.readthedocs.io/en/latest/proposals/0631-main-return-types.html>`_.
